+# Flight 77 call windows in the filed stipulation and March 7 transcript
+
+Public derivative of the November 10, 2026 source review. TEL02–TEL04 / AUD016-A1 / TC05–TC06. The filed scan places two reported conversations in separate overlapping windows. A public reproduction of the March 7 trial transcript renders the same four endpoints as point-time wording. Commission endnote 57 reports four connected records with unknown numbers, while the later Flight 77 presentation contains a separately named zero-duration entry. Preserve these statements and representations side by side. The event-to-person and operator-to-recipient joins remain open.
+
+## Filed text and trial reading
+
+| Source and locator | First clause | Second clause |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| **ST00001 Part A** ¶3(k)–(l), printed and physical pp. **7–8** | **“Between 9:15 a.m. and 9:26 a.m.”** One reported conversation with her husband, described as about one minute before cutoff. | **“Between 9:20 a.m. and 9:31 a.m.”** Describes calling again and speaking to him. The continuation about the call is on p. 8. |
+| **Volume II-A** March 7, 2006, p. **330** lines **19–25** and p. **331** lines **1–5** | **“At 9:15 a.m. and at 9:26 a.m.”** The reproduced clause still uses singular call/cutoff wording and says about one minute. | **“At 9:20 a.m. and 9:31 a.m.”** The reproduced clause continues into p. 331. |
+
+The exhibit page calls the two-part file a stipulation. The archived Part A scan has a **March 1, 2006** filing stamp and exhibit stamp **ST00001**. Volume II-A p. **318** line **3** identifies **ST-1** in evidence. At p. **329** lines **5–8**, counsel returns to the stipulation and identifies p. **6** ¶**3**. This supplies a document-level link for the Flight 77 reading. The archived document p. 6 begins ¶3 and the selected call passages follow on pp. 7–8. The timing phrases above differ literally. Whether the difference arose in what was read, what was transcribed, the version used in court, or an HTML conversion remains unresolved. The ordered number of native calls cannot be derived from the number of minute labels in the reproduced reading. [Court exhibit index](https://coop.vaed.uscourts.gov/moussaoui/exhibits/prosecution/ST00001.html) · [Archived court scan, p. 7](https://web.archive.org/web/20190207163520/http://www.vaed.uscourts.gov/notablecases/moussaoui/exhibits/prosecution/ST00001A.pdf#page=7) · [Volume II-A public reproduction](https://cryptome.wikileaks.org/usa-v-zm-030706-02.htm)
+
+A separate wording control in the same sources has **9:24 a.m.** for receipt of the UA93 dispatcher warning at ST00001 Part A ¶4(c), p. **9**, and **8:24 a.m.** at Volume II-A p. **334**, line **9**. Both give **9:26 a.m.** for the following cockpit reply. Preserve the two receive values. This comparison tests document fidelity and supplies no clock correction or assessment of the actual aircraft messaging sequence. The printed ¶3 second-clause marker reads **l.** on the page face, while the previously saved page OCR renders **1.** at line 27. [Archived scan, p. 9](https://web.archive.org/web/20190207163520/http://www.vaed.uscourts.gov/notablecases/moussaoui/exhibits/prosecution/ST00001A.pdf#page=9) · [Volume II-A, p. 334](https://cryptome.wikileaks.org/usa-v-zm-030706-02.htm)
+
+## Reproducible time-window test
+
+Endnote **57**, official HTML raw line **135**, lists **9:15:34 / 1:42**, **9:20:15 / 4:34**, **9:25:48 / 2:34** and **9:30:56 / 4:20**. It describes four connected calls to unknown numbers, says the records leave unresolved which two represent conversations between the Olsons, and separately reports FBI/DOJ's belief that all four were communications with the office. Retain the unknown-number designation and the agency belief together. This is a Commission account citing its underlying records. [Commission endnote 57](https://www.911commission.gov/report/911Report_Notes.htm)
+
+Under a provisional same-clock comparison, these are the memberships of the printed windows. Treating the upper printed minute as an exact :00 endpoint or including the full terminal minute gives the same memberships for these four records.
+
+| Printed window | Endnote 57 starts inside it |
+| --- | --- |
+| 9:15–9:26 | 9:15:34, 9:20:15, 9:25:48 |
+| 9:20–9:31 | 9:20:15, 9:25:48, 9:30:56 |
+
+Even requiring two distinct rows in chronological order leaves **six possible pairs** by time alone. Sorting the four reproduced minute labels and subtracting the four endnote times in order gives **−34, −15, +12 and +4 seconds**. Those differences are arithmetic on displayed values. They leave clock synchronization, rounding conventions, call start versus conversation time, and source dependence open. The test supplies no caller assignment. It also leaves the separately preserved **154 versus 159 seconds** for the 9:25:48 record unresolved. [Commission endnote 57](https://www.911commission.gov/report/911Report_Notes.htm) · [Earlier Flight 77 source comparison](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/2d73a93d12276caae2b6029eff5c504bfdb8ff3b/investigation/broader-evidence/telephone-zero-entry-context-verified-2026-11-02/README.md)
+
+The presentation **P200054** encodes the separate **09:18:58**, `0 SECONDS `, `DEPARTMENT OF JUSTICEUNCONNECTED CALL` entry in a structure with Barbara Olson's name. It lies inside the first printed window and outside the second if read on the same clock. The exhibit text describes an unconnected event. The stipulation describes conversations. Neither timing compatibility nor the label establishes how the carrier or operator represented attempted, connected and transferred legs. Preserve the September 20 analysis's unnamed office-connection account and the distinct later unconnected label. [Court exhibit](https://coop.vaed.uscourts.gov/moussaoui/exhibits/prosecution/flights/P200054.html) · [Verified SWF placement and remaining conflicts](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/2d73a93d12276caae2b6029eff5c504bfdb8ff3b/investigation/broader-evidence/telephone-zero-entry-context-verified-2026-11-02/README.md)
+
+## Acquisition and open tests
+
+The court docket lists **1668**, **March 7, 2006 at 1:30 p.m.**, **Volume II-A**, filed **March 10**. Its link exposes a one-page access notice. The public reproduction labels the same date, session and volume. Its main preformatted text has consecutive page labels **238–392**, and includes a certification page in transcription. Original signed reporter bytes and any corrections to the reading remain unacquired. The first transcript host returned **403**, and that hash is for the error page. The mirror returned **200**. The Commission HTML and held Part A bytes were hash-verified, and selected Part A images and prior OCR checked. Verification reproduced seven transcript anchors, six scan OCR anchors, four endnote rows and six ordered time-only pairings. [Court docket, entry 1668](https://coop.vaed.uscourts.gov/moussaoui/dktsheets/DocketSheet2.html) · [Public access notice](https://coop.vaed.uscourts.gov/moussaoui/dktsheets/docs/71810/0.pdf) · [Public transcript mirror](https://cryptome.wikileaks.org/usa-v-zm-030706-02.htm)
+
+- [ ] **TEL02.** Obtain the clerk/reporter copy for entry **1668**, the version of ST-1 used in the reading, and any correction or revised exhibit. Compare the exact timing phrases and their source representations before using point-time language as a court finding.
+- [ ] **TEL02–TEL04.** Obtain the source-to-exhibit and source-to-stipulation worksheets, the original carrier and operator/office records with leg identifiers, and the underlying interview and usage-report sources. Test who made or received each call only with event, service, routing, connection and recipient evidence. The signed FAA correction and disposition, and the other work-plan tracks, remain open.
